ask(c,'Why is selective compliance useful for vertical insertion?', ['Relative lateral compliance can accommodate small alignment errors while vertical stiffness supports insertion','Vertical compliance is maximized while horizontal motion is completely locked','All four joints must be passive during insertion','The arm must have equal stiffness in every direction'],['The source contrasts compliant X–Y motion with relatively stiff Z behavior.','This reverses the stated directional behavior.','Selective compliance does not require disabling all joint actuation.','The defining feature is directional, not isotropic, behavior.'])
