ask(c,'For an unrestricted planar two-link arm with fixed total reach L=l1+l2, which length choice maximizes the geometric annular area?', ['l1=l2=L/2','l1/l2=1.5 for every value of L','l2 approaches zero','Any ratio gives the same area'],['Area is π[(l1+l2)²−(l1−l2)²]=4πl1l2; at fixed sum the product is largest for equal lengths.','The source’s 1.3–1.5 recommendation cannot be a universal maximum for this specified metric.','A vanishing second link makes the annular area approach zero.','The product changes with the ratio.'],difficulty='medium',pages=[611,618],conflict=(611,'A length ratio of about 1.3–1.5 optimises dexterous workspace area.','The optimum depends on the dexterity metric and constraints. For unrestricted geometric annular area at fixed total length, equal lengths maximize 4πl1l2.'),assumptions=['Positive link lengths, fixed sum, unrestricted planar rotations and geometric position area rather than a separately defined dexterity metric.'])
