ask(c,'A table lists ±0.01 mm repeatability. Which conclusion does that alone justify?', ['It describes repeated-position consistency under the specified test conditions, not guaranteed absolute calibration accuracy','It proves every commanded point is within±0.01 mm of its true world position','It proves the robot has no backlash, thermal drift or calibration error','It proves the camera has±0.01 mm measurement accuracy'],['Repeatability and absolute accuracy are separate performance concepts.','A repeatable robot can have systematic position bias.','The scalar specification does not prove absence of every error source.','The robot’s repeatability does not specify camera accuracy.'],difficulty='medium')
c=concept(625,'Vision-coordinate integration and condition monitoring','Detection-to-motion pipeline and maintenance signals.')
ask(c,'Which sequence matches the lecture’s vision-guided motion description?', ['Localize a part in camera data, transform its pose into robot coordinates, then solve IK','Solve IK on raw pixel coordinates, then determine camera calibration afterward','Convert motor current directly into barcode text, then skip localization','Apply the target yaw only, without determining the target position'],['The detected pose must be expressed in the frame used by the robot’s kinematics.','Pixels are not directly interchangeable with physical robot coordinates.','Motor-current monitoring is a different function from visual identification.','Pick-and-place requires position as well as the chosen orientation.'],kind='sequence')
ask(c,'Which set contains only vision uses explicitly listed in this section?', ['Part localization, barcode identification, defect inspection and flexible-feeder guidance','Bearing lubrication, winding cooling, gear cutting and shaft balancing','Joint-current regulation, brake release, power conversion and fuse selection','Encoder homing, screw pitch selection, torque sizing and casting manufacture'],['These are all named image-based applications.','These are maintenance/manufacturing operations, not the listed visual tasks.','These are electrical/actuation functions rather than the listed vision capabilities.','These are robot setup/design tasks, not the source’s vision-use set.'])
ask(c,'Which monitoring signals are listed for fault diagnosis and maintenance scheduling?', ['Motor current, joint position, joint velocity, temperature and vibration','Only commanded tool coordinates, with all measured signals discarded','Only camera megapixel count and nominal reach','Only the purchase prices of motors and reducers'],['The lecture explicitly lists these five measured quantities.','Condition monitoring uses measured operating behavior, not merely commands.','Static specification values do not replace the listed operating signals.','Costs are BOM data, not health measurements.'])
ask(c,'How does gearbox/bearing condition monitoring support availability?', ['It can reveal degradation and inform maintenance before unexpected downtime','It guarantees that mechanical components can never fail','It replaces all servo feedback measurements','It changes the robot’s kinematic joint sequence'],['The stated goal is diagnosis and scheduling, not an absolute prevention guarantee.','Monitoring does not eliminate all failure mechanisms.','Control feedback and health monitoring have related but distinct roles.','Monitoring does not convert RRPR into another physical architecture.'],kind='scenario')
