ask(c,'What inconsistency appears between the task statement and the requirements table?', ['The part is0.5 g on one page but0.5 kg on the next, a factor1000 difference','The gripper is0.8 kg on both pages but must therefore be massless','The cover dimensions change from152×72 mm to152×72 cm','The required positional tolerance changes from±0.1 mm to±10 mm'],['0.5 kg equals500 g, not0.5 g.','The0.8 kg gripper is not a contradiction of zero mass.','The source does not print that dimensional change.','The required tolerance remains±0.1 mm in the supplied statements.'],pages=[627,628],conflict=(627,'The cover mass is printed as0.5 g; the next page budgets0.5 kg for the part.','The two values differ by1000. Each numerical question explicitly selects one mass scenario; no unstated correction is imposed.'))
ask(c,'If the literal0.5 g part statement and a0.8 kg gripper are used together, what combined moving payload mass results?', ['0.8005 kg','1.3 kg','0.805 kg','500.8 kg'],['0.5 g=0.0005 kg, so the sum is0.8005 kg.','This instead uses the next page’s0.5 kg part value.','This converts0.5 g as5 g.','This multiplies0.5 g by1000 instead of dividing by1000 to convert to kilograms.'],kind='numerical',pages=[627,628],steps=['Convert grams to kilograms by dividing by1000.','0.5 g=0.0005 kg.','Add0.8 kg to obtain0.8005 kg.'],assumptions=['This uses the literal0.5 g scenario, not the conflicting0.5 kg table scenario.'])
issue(627,'payload-mass-unit','The part mass changes from0.5 g to0.5 kg on consecutive pages.','Retain both literal values; every calculation explicitly declares which scenario it uses.')
